# UST.G3DV H02 Final Eight-Prime Holdout Theorem v1

## Status

`CLOSED_EXACT_SEVEN_PRIME_RECONSTRUCTION_WITH_FINAL_EIGHTH_PRIME_HOLDOUT`

G3DV exhausts the eight completely split primes already persisted by G3BU.
It reconstructs every normalized H02 kernel coefficient from the first seven
prime archives and tests it against the eighth archive, prime 73,673, which is
not consulted during candidate construction.

All 48 roots across the eight primes have exact bordered rank 29,515, coupling
rank 4,748, nullity 1,274 and one common selected/dependent coordinate
partition. The coefficient audit separately records stable candidates and
rejected CRT aliases.

## Boundary and next proof form

The normalized dense kernel is a determinant-ratio representation. Its large
coefficient heights make repeated prime extension an inefficient final proof
strategy. Even an eighth-prime holdout remains finite evidence and is not an
identity over `Q(gamma)`.

The next exact theorem should exploit the frozen 34-component update order.
All 1,274 dependent coordinates occur in only 16 components, several of which
are entirely dependent. A componentwise rank-upper certificate can therefore
replace millions of dense reconstructed fractions with a small collection of
exact local identities or rank factorizations.

G3DV does not prove characteristic-zero rank 4,748, the second Woodbury
factorization, H02 source contraction, path integration, integral marking,
readout or `beta_C`.

